      "message": "\u003e The trick with MSL is that we don\u0027t emit the return builtins in the function signature (sorry, missed this earlier), they all get packed in to a return structure. So, we should have created the return structure with the attributes attached (they\u0027re then stripped from the function itself).\n\n\u003e So, for the return this should all be bundled up into the return struct already. Which I\u0027d expect your change below in the EmitStructType to have emitted the depth, so either the attribute is not copying correct in the IOAttributes or something else is going wrong?\n\nFYI `Resolver::Structure()` (which contains the following code) is not called when parsing `basic.wgsl` while it is for `struct.wgsl`.\n\n```cpp\n                [\u0026](const ast::BuiltinAttribute* attr) {\n                    attributes.builtin \u003d attr-\u003ebuiltin;\n                    attributes.depth_mode \u003d attr-\u003edepth_mode;\n                    return true;\n                },\n```",
